From 8d4650ec88cebbef25aec5451a484dc65100489e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:41:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] Dolby Vision that does not go out natively goes
 at its own rate with VRR, as HDR10+ does

VRR_VIDEO::Decide() refused every video that said it was Dolby Vision,
whatever went out. On a display without Dolby Vision, or where the user
chose another output, a Dolby Vision video goes out as HDR10, HDR10+ or
SDR: a profile 7 film rebuilt and sent as
HDR10+ to a Samsung Odyssey G60SD went at a fixed 359.999 Hz with
"Always". It is now taken as HDR10+ is: only where the driver sends
HDR10+ next to the VRR packet (NV_HDR10PLUS_WITH_VRR, Ada and
Blackwell), with the same checks of VRR, and not where it may go out as
HLG (its stream or its base layer is HLG: DVBRIDGE::StreamOutputMayBeHlg(),
profiles 8.4 and 10.4). CHdmiVrrOff::Wanted() already counted Dolby
Vision sent as HDR10+.

Native Dolby Vision stays out, now with its reason
(NativeDolbyVisionWhy()), looked at for the LG C5: its transport is
3840x2160 at a CTA rate from 23.976 to 60 Hz (IsTransportMode()), so
from menus at 120 Hz a change of mode comes anyway; no display declares
Dolby Vision with VRR (neither the Dolby block nor the HDMI Forum block
has a field for it); and a display that did not decode the tunnel at a
varying refresh would show a wrong picture that no check of the source
can see. With "Always" a native Dolby Vision video is refused before
Kodi's choice and is not asked again after it (AskedAfterKodi(), in
CResolutionUtils::ChooseBestResolution()): it gets its change of mode
to its rate, never the fixed refresh of the menus.
